      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Disabling Pinch Gestures or being able to toggle specific ones on and off would be great for the StretchSense Reality XR Game gloves I recently received.\n\nAll of the existing VRC Pinch Gestures are constantly fighting against this glove's software which emulates Index Controller bindings via additive ML pose sets.\n\nThe option to selectively use some of VRC's implementations (like the pressable menu button on the wrist) alongside these glove's own bindings would be ideal to allow the user the freedom to set up their control scheme as needed.\n\nAs-is, they aren't very usable since VRC's own bindings will be triggering constantly with any gestures close to those existing ones.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2024-08-17T06:58:26.506Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Currently, with Steam Input 2.0 & Hand Tracking Only (E.G. Steam Link beta on Meta Quest), there is no way to disable the entire set of pinch bindings (the ones displayed by Pinch UI). Additionally, some of these cannot be mapped via Steam Input (e.g. I cannot remap the pinch movement used by VRChat in Steam Input for Hand Tracking Controllers; As hand tracking controllers provide no vector-2 based inputs I cannot use existing movement actions.) **Index gestures also interfere with SteamVR overlay input, which cannot be remapped.**\n\nPlease expose the full set of Pinch UI actions to Steam Input, and allow for Pinch Gestures to be disabled entirely beyond what is mapped via Steam.\n\nThe current system is convoluted and confusing, as now half the options are either VRChat settings, or not (re)bindable at all, while the other half are all bound via SteamVR.",
